messages:
alex: FYI some customers are getting 415s when calling /v2/completions if they send `Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8`. Noticed in a couple support tickets.

tara: that sounds like a content-type parsing mismatch. we should accept standard params on json media types. are we currently doing an exact string compare anywhere? @mike any pointers to the proxy middleware?

mike: digging in now. we switched a middleware recently that normalizes headers to lowercase and started doing exact equality checks downstream. this will fail if clients include charset or other params. :grimacing:

priya: i can reproduce with curl locally. server returns 415 unless header is exactly `application/json`.

alex: proposal: update the proxy to match only the type/subtype and ignore parameters for application/json. ensure we still distinguish application/x-ndjson for streaming endpoints.

mike: agree. plan: parse content-type, then compare the mime type portion. quick patch example:
```
const { parse } = require('content-type');
let mimeType = 'unknown';
try {
  mimeType = parse(headers['content-type']).type;
} catch (e) {
  mimeType = headers['content-type']?.split(';')[0]?.trim().toLowerCase();
}
if (mimeType === 'application/json' || mimeType === 'application/x-ndjson') {
  // proceed
} else {
  return 415;
}
```

tara: nice. also add a small helper util we can reuse so other services don't repeat brittle checks.

priya: tests i ran: `application/json;charset=utf-8`, `application/json; charset=UTF-8`, mixed case `Application/JSON`, and `application/json ; foo=bar` all should be accepted. failing case: `text/plain; charset=utf-8` should still 415.

mike: i'll open a PR with the fix + unit tests covering those permutations and a tiny integration canary against staging.

mike: PR 498 opened: https://github.com/redwood-inference/proxy/pull/498 (includes tests and a small content-type util)

deploy-bot: canary deploy started for proxy PR #498 to staging - build 202405. monitor /v2/completions for 415 rates.

priya: canary smoke looks good on staging. curl example now succeeds:
```
curl -i -X POST https://staging.api.redwood.ai/v2/completions \ 
  -H \"Content-Type: application/json; charset=utf-8\" \ 
  -d '{"model":"gpt-small","prompt":"hello"}'
```

alex: great. follow-ups:
- add a short note in API docs explaining we accept standard media type params for application/json
- add a linter rule or code review checklist item to avoid exact string equality checks on content-type
- backport to any other services that did exact matching

mike: opened issue #821 to add a lint sniff for exact equality checks on content-type in middleware repos. will ship the doc blurb in next docs sprint.

tara: thanks all. leaving this thread, feel free to @channel in infra if we see any regressions. :+1:
